{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "uniform_regret_cluster_balance",
  "intent": "Address the parent's uniform-instance weakness by inverting the regret-cluster_density coupling: regret now DECREASES with cd, so uniform instances (low cd) get stronger regret-k guidance where it's most needed, while clustered instances rely more on density signals. Flatten the return progress ramp slightly and add a small nearest_remaining penalty to prefer candidates that lead smoothly into remaining nodes, improving continuation. Distance remains the dominant anchor; all coefficients stay within [0.07, 0.45] to preserve the parent's cluster and grid strengths.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "cluster"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    reg = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    return -d + (0.1 + 0.3 * p) * (1 - 0.3 * cd) * rd + (0.35 + 0.1 * p - 0.1 * cd) * reg - 0.08 * nr",
